# .copilotignore
#
# Prevents AI coding assistants (GitHub Copilot and compatible agents/extensions
# that honour this file) from reading sensitive files as context.
#
# Syntax: .gitignore-style glob patterns, one per line; "#" starts a comment.
#
# NOTE ON ENFORCEMENT
# This file is honoured by tools that support the community `.copilotignore`
# convention. GitHub Copilot's *authoritative* protection is "content exclusion",
# configured in repository/organisation settings on GitHub — configure the same
# patterns there as well:
# https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/how-tos/configure-content-exclusion/exclude-content-from-copilot
# Keep this list and the content-exclusion settings in sync. Never rely on this
# file alone to protect a real secret — secrets must not be committed at all
# (see DEFRA credential-exposure process).

# --- Environment & local config (may contain secrets) ---
.env
.env.*
*.env
!*.example.env
!.env.example
.envrc
compose/*.env

# --- Secrets, credentials & tokens ---
**/secret*
**/*secret*
**/*secrets*
secrets.json
credentials
credentials.*
**/credentials/**
.npmrc
.netrc
.pgpass

# --- Keys & certificates ---
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.truststore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.gpg
*.asc
*.ppk

# --- Cloud / infrastructure credentials & state ---
.aws/**
**/aws.env
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars

# --- Session / auth material ---
*.cookie
session-secret*
